<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena outlines vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 1) (Lagena spp. (monothalamic Foraminifera), 13 specimens figured by Thompson after Brady (1884))",
        "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena outlines vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Lagena spp. (monothalamic Foraminifera), 13 specimens figured by Thompson after Brady (1884) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean, morphoeval/math_kg_loops/thompson1917-t1917-014.yaml implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Lagena spp. (monothalamic Foraminifera), 13 specimens figured by Thompson after Brady (1884) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/math_kg_loops/thompson1917-t1917-014.yaml>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py> ;
    schema:about "Lagena spp. (monothalamic Foraminifera), 13 specimens figured by Thompson after Brady (1884)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: No claim about the surface-tension mechanism (hanging drop); no claim about Nodosaria chains, Orbulina or non-foram protists; no statistical test beyond RMSE / Pearson r in this pass",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Kenmotsu (1980) parametrisation of the Delaunay family; C1 sphere-unduloid-cylinder flask and unduloid bead composites fitted by bounded least squares to the meridional radius profile of each of the 13 Fig. 84 silhouettes",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) p. 256: Lagena shells are 'flask-shaped ... whose surface is simply that of an unduloid, or more frequently ... an unduloid combined with a portion of a sphere'; p. 218: the CMC surfaces of revolution are the plane, sphere, cylinder, catenoid, unduloid and nodoid",
        "transfer_boundary: The silhouettes are Brady's drawings as redrawn in 1917, not photographs; pixel edge noise is 2-4 % of r_max; no modern specimen has been analysed yet" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/math_kg_loops/thompson1917-t1917-014.yaml; output: docs/media/t1917_014_the_forms_of_cells_comparison.png; organism: Lagena spp. (monothalamic Foraminifera), 13 specimens figured by Thompson after Brady (1884); environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) p. 256: Lagena shells are 'flask-shaped ... whose surface is simply that of an unduloid, or more frequently ... an unduloid combined with a portion of a sphere'; p. 218: the CMC surfaces of revolution are the plane, sphere, cylinder, catenoid, unduloid and nodoid; reconstructed_in_script: Kenmotsu (1980) parametrisation of the Delaunay family; C1 sphere-unduloid-cylinder flask and unduloid bead composites fitted by bounded least squares to the meridional radius profile of each of the 13 Fig. 84 silhouettes; transfer_boundary: The silhouettes are Brady's drawings as redrawn in 1917, not photographs; pixel edge noise is 2-4 % of r_max; no modern specimen has been analysed yet; does_not_claim: No claim about the surface-tension mechanism (hanging drop); no claim about Nodosaria chains, Orbulina or non-foram protists; no statistical test beyond RMSE / Pearson r in this pass]; other sources: On Growth and Form (1st ed.), Ch. V The Forms of Cells, pp. 201-276 <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, Sur la surface de révolution dont la courbure moyenne est constante <http://www.numdam.org/item/JMPA_1841_1_6__309_0/>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.2748/tmj/1178229688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.10.e87457>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.28816> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-014-the-forms-of-cells-audit-thompson1917-t1917-014-8> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Constant-Mean-Curvature Surfaces of Revolution (Delaunay 1841 / Plateau catalogue: sphere, cylinder, unduloid, nodoid, catenoid) — geometric" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.08e-01 .

