<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena outlines vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 1) — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every function docstring names the equation id (E3-E8) and the Thompson page it implements; the Lean module and math KG YAML cite the exact script line ranges. The decision threshold 0.06 is a stated judgement, not derived from a noise model." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py L72–L73: RMSE_SUPPORT = 0.06 justified only by a comment <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L72-L73>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena outlines vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 1) — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The catalogue is implemented from the first-integral / Kenmotsu form with the correct limits (cylinder, unduloid, spheres, nodoid, catenoid), self-tested against the root identities and the elliptic-integral period, and 18 Lean theorems check the integer algebra (roots, envelope, trichotomy, bead bound, flask join). Thompson's flask qualification is honoured by the C1 composite. Deductions: the flask's sphere-unduloid join is restricted to the one-parameter family of C1 joins (no C2 matching), the neck is a plain cylinder with no apertural lip, and the nodoid is classified but never fitted." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py L154–L176: join is C1 only and the neck is an idealised cylinder without lip <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L154-L176>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena outlines vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 1) — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Quantitative morphometrics are computed on every silhouette (L/W, asymmetry index, fitted B, neck ratio, nRMSE, Pearson r) and the bead aspect bound gives an a priori prediction (L/W <= pi) that is checked. There is no null model (ellipsoid), no free-form reference to calibrate the noise floor, no KS test or cross-validation, and no literature measurement of Lagena dimensions." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py L250–L258: only nRMSE and Pearson r are implemented <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L250-L258>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-delaunay-compatible-specimens-best-catalogue-fit-nrmse-0-06>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-fig-84-lagena-silhouettes-segmented>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-fitted-kenmotsu-b-range>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-best-fit-rmse-r-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-best-fit-rmse-r-max-flask-like-l-w-pi>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-best-fit-rmse-r-max-spindles-l-w-pi>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-bilateral-asymmetry-index-mean-r-l-r-r-r-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-measurement-median-pearson-r-observed-vs-fitted-radius>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena outlines vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 60.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "v1 implements the Delaunay catalogue exactly (Kenmotsu E4, neck-ratio E5, period E6, catenoid), builds Thompson's 'unduloid + portion of a sphere' as a C1 composite (E7) plus a pure unduloid bead (E8), segments all 13 Lagena of Fig. 84 and fits both models. Result: 6/13 Delaunay-compatible at the 0.06 gate; flask-like specimens (L/W <= pi, n = 8) median nRMSE 0.049, spindles (L/W > pi, n = 5) median 0.209; median bilateral asymmetry 0.058. Missing: photograph of a real specimen, null and free-form comparators, statistics (KS / CV), parameter sweep, negative control, verdict file. Overall 60.8/100 (faithfulness 54.1, reproducibility 76.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d762bb9c6; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 45, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_014_the_forms_of_cells_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py at d762bb9c6, image/png, 634068 B, 2200×1430 px, artifact_sha256 500c908720bfbd2b6bd41fcef910785ff899c148c871a9adeeb18378a469a4c2 (sha256 500c908720bfbd2b6bd41fcef910785ff899c148c871a9adeeb18378a469a4c2), spec_fingerprint ce11ca3725361e46a837bbcd24fc0d74234556b6328d06d635521b2bb17dd6e7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ce11ca3725361e46a837bbcd24fc0d74234556b6328d06d635521b2bb17dd6e7; artifact_sha256: 500c908720bfbd2b6bd41fcef910785ff899c148c871a9adeeb18378a469a4c2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/kireenko_2022_bdj_e87457_fig8_station5656mc.jpg=3b57acc0dfc98374..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/paper_citations.bib=a21c514d2fded5d2..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/scout_manifest.json=53e6b01a4f0e6102..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/t1917_014_the_forms_of_cells_reference.json=0a5ac92486643991..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/thompson_1917_fig84_lagena_after_brady.png=c02d29af384791df..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/thompson_1917_leaf0276_p256_fig84.jp2=ed440583a8b144d5...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) p. 256: Lagena shells are 'flask-shaped ... whose surface is simply that of an unduloid, or more frequently ... an unduloid combined with a portion of a sphere'; p. 218: the CMC surfaces of revolution are the plane, sphere, cylinder, catenoid, unduloid and nodoid; reconstructed_in_script: Kenmotsu (1980) parametrisation of the Delaunay family; C1 sphere-unduloid-cylinder flask and unduloid bead composites fitted by bounded least squares to the meridional radius profile of each of the 13 Fig. 84 silhouettes; transfer_boundary: The silhouettes are Brady's drawings as redrawn in 1917, not photographs; pixel edge noise is 2-4 % of r_max; no modern specimen has been analysed yet; does_not_claim: No claim about the surface-tension mechanism (hanging drop); no claim about Nodosaria chains, Orbulina or non-foram protists; no statistical test beyond RMSE / Pearson r in this pass." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different provider) — this round is builder-scored'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Segment the real specimens in the vendored Kireenko (2022) CC-BY plate (Lagena 61a/62a, Oolina 63, Fissurina 57a/58a) and fit them with the same pipeline; report sizes in um from the 100 um scale bars'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Add the ellipsoid null model and a free-form (degree-6 r^2 polynomial) reference so the Delaunay residual is judged against the attainable noise floor, not a fixed 0.06'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Add statistics: KS test between observed and fitted radius distributions, 2-fold cross-validated RMSE, Pearson r per model'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Negative/ablation control: fit the Delaunay models to polythalamous tests on the same plate (Globobulimina 64a, Quinqueloculina 66a), which the claim does not cover and which should fit worse'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Parameter-regime sweep: tabulate neck ratio, period and bead aspect ratio over B in [0, 1.5] (cylinder -> unduloid -> spheres -> nodoid) and the flask join feasibility over t'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': 'Write datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-014/result.json with the claim verdict (supported | refuted | mixed | untestable) and headline numbers'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.08e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-014-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-014 — Lagena outlines vs. the Plateau/Delaunay catalogue (Pass 1) — Parameter expressivity: 50/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "B visibly and monotonically controls the neck ratio in the GIF (cylinder to string of spheres) and the flask neck length grows with L_neck; the fitted B per specimen spans 0.30-0.85. No systematic sweep over (B, t, L_neck) is tabulated, the nodoid branch (B > 1) and the catenoid are only drawn, and no CLI exposes the parameters." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
