<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Delaunay first integral — neck/bulge root identities" ;
    dct:description "Fixes the two turning radii of every unduloid from (H, C); used by kenmotsu_profile and checked numerically in self_test | Variables: a: semi-major axis of Delaunay's rolling ellipse (= 1/(2H)); c: focal half-distance; r_max = a + c bulge radius; r_min = a - c neck radius" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) pp. 216-219 (Laplace formula, Delaunay 1841 footnote, Fig. 61); Delaunay (1841) J. Math. Pures Appl. 6:309" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean#L32-L69>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L124-L136> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def rMax (a c : Int) : Int := a + c
def rMin (a c : Int) : Int := a - c
theorem roots_sum (a c : Int) : rMax a c + rMin a c = 2 * a
theorem roots_product (a c : Int) : rMax a c * rMin a c = a * a - c * c
theorem first_integral_turning_points (a c : Int) :
    rMax a c * rMax a c - rMin a c * rMin a c = 2 * a * (rMax a c - rMin a c)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r/sqrt(1+r'^2) - H r^2 = C;  r_min + r_max = 1/H = 2a;  r_min r_max = C/H = a^2 - c^2 = b^2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.2748/tmj/1178229688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.10.e87457>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.28816> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Constant-Mean-Curvature Surfaces of Revolution (Delaunay 1841 / Plateau catalogue: sphere, cylinder, unduloid, nodoid, catenoid) — geometric" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.rMax" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.roots_product" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Neck-ratio law of the unduloid family" ;
    dct:description "Single shape parameter of the unduloid up to scale; the fitted B is reported per specimen and swept in the GIF (cylinder -> unduloid -> spheres) | Variables: B = c/a: Kenmotsu parameter = eccentricity of the rolling ellipse" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) p. 218: 'the more unequal the two axes are of our ellipse, the more pronounced will be the sinuosity of the described roulette'" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean#L72-L105>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L108-L111> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem neck_between (a c : Int) (h0 : 0 ≤ c) (h1 : c ≤ a) : 0 ≤ rMin a c ∧ rMin a c ≤ rMax a c
theorem cylinder_limit (a : Int) : rMin a 0 = rMax a 0
theorem sphere_limit (a : Int) : rMin a a = 0
theorem neck_ratio_strict_anti (a c₁ c₂ : Int) (ha : 0 < a) (h : c₁ < c₂) :
    rMin a c₂ * rMax a c₁ < rMin a c₁ * rMax a c₂
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "rho = r_min/r_max = (1 - B)/(1 + B) = (a - c)/(a + c); 0 <= rho <= 1, strictly decreasing in c; rho = 1 cylinder, rho = 0 string of spheres" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.2748/tmj/1178229688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.10.e87457>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.28816> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Constant-Mean-Curvature Surfaces of Revolution (Delaunay 1841 / Plateau catalogue: sphere, cylinder, unduloid, nodoid, catenoid) — geometric" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.rMin" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.neck_ratio_strict_anti" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kenmotsu radius envelope (CMC surface of revolution)" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees the meridian stays within [r_min, r_max]; mirrors the envelope assertion in self_test | Variables: S: integer scale of the sine (σ = S sin 2Hs); B in [0, S]" ;
    dct:source "Kenmotsu (1980) Tohoku Math. J. 32:147-153, eq. (2.4); Thompson (1917) p. 223 on the unduloid's curvature sum staying positive and constant" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean#L108-L122>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L124-L146> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem kenmotsu_envelope (S B σ : Int) (hB0 : 0 ≤ B) (hσl : -S ≤ σ) (hσu : σ ≤ S) :
    (S - B) * (S - B) ≤ S * S + B * B + 2 * (B * σ) ∧
    S * S + B * B + 2 * (B * σ) ≤ (S + B) * (S + B)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "(2H r)^2 = 1 + B^2 + 2B sin(2Hs);  (1-B)^2 <= (2Hr)^2 <= (1+B)^2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.2748/tmj/1178229688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.10.e87457>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.28816> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Constant-Mean-Curvature Surfaces of Revolution (Delaunay 1841 / Plateau catalogue: sphere, cylinder, unduloid, nodoid, catenoid) — geometric" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.kenmotsu_envelope" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.kenmotsu_envelope" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Plateau/Delaunay catalogue trichotomy" ;
    dct:description "The 'very few in number' surfaces Thompson lists on p. 218; classify_delaunay in the script | Variables: B scaled by S" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) pp. 218-219, Figs. 61-65; Plateau (1873) Statique des liquides" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean#L125-L150>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L95-L105> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def catalogue (S B : Int) : Nat :=
  if B = 0 then 0 else if B < S then 1 else if B = S then 2 else 3
theorem catalogue_unduloid (S B : Int) (h0 : 0 < B) (h1 : B < S) : catalogue S B = 1
theorem catalogue_exhaustive (S B : Int) :
    catalogue S B = 0 ∨ catalogue S B = 1 ∨ catalogue S B = 2 ∨ catalogue S B = 3
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "B = 0 cylinder; 0 < B < 1 unduloid; B = 1 string of spheres; B > 1 nodoid; H = 0 catenoid" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.2748/tmj/1178229688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.10.e87457>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.28816> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Constant-Mean-Curvature Surfaces of Revolution (Delaunay 1841 / Plateau catalogue: sphere, cylinder, unduloid, nodoid, catenoid) — geometric" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.catalogue" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.catalogue_exhaustive" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Unduloid bead aspect-ratio bound (refutation lemma for fusiform Lagena)" ;
    dct:description "Shows a priori that the slender spindles of Fig. 84 (L/W 5-11) cannot be single unduloids; bead_aspect_ratio in the script | Variables: L: axial bead length; P: meridian arc length over one period (= pi/H); W: bead width 2 r_max; scale 1000 = 1/H" ;
    dct:source "Consequence of Kenmotsu (1980) dz/ds = cos psi <= 1; Thompson (1917) p. 256 'simply that of an unduloid' tested" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean#L156-L173>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L113-L122> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem bead_aspect_bound (L P W : Int) (hL : L ≤ P) (hP : P ≤ 3142) (hW : 1000 ≤ W) :
    1000 * L ≤ 3142 * W
theorem spindle_not_bead (L W : Int) (hW : 1000 ≤ W) (h : 3142 * W < 1000 * L) :
    ¬ ∃ P : Int, L ≤ P ∧ P ≤ 3142
theorem fig84_spindle_3_not_bead : ¬ ∃ P : Int, (10940 : Int) ≤ P ∧ P ≤ 3142
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L_bead <= pi/H (arc length), W = (1+B)/H >= 1/H  =>  L/W <= pi;  exact value 2E(e)/(1+e)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.2748/tmj/1178229688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.10.e87457>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.28816> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Constant-Mean-Curvature Surfaces of Revolution (Delaunay 1841 / Plateau catalogue: sphere, cylinder, unduloid, nodoid, catenoid) — geometric" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.bead_aspect_bound" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.spindle_not_bead" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-014-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Delaunay flask C1 join (sphere + unduloid + cylinder)" ;
    dct:description "Makes Thompson's 'unduloid combined with a portion of a sphere' a well-posed 5-parameter model (flask_profile) | Variables: R: sphere radius; H, B: unduloid; kappa = RH in [(1-B)/2, (1+B)/2]; k = S kappa" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) p. 256 (Lagena), p. 257 (Darling's hanging drops 'unduloids with spherical ends'), p. 226 Fig. 67 (cylinder capped by spheres)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_014.lean#L176-L221>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d762bb9c6/thompson/claims/t1917-014_the-forms-of-cells.py#L154-L184> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """theorem flask_equator_join (S B : Int) : (S + B) * (2 * S - (S + B)) = S * S - B * B
theorem flask_join_feasible (S B k : Int) (hk1 : S - B ≤ 2 * k) (hk2 : 2 * k ≤ S + B) :
    S * S - B * B ≤ 4 * (k * (S - k))
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r_j^2 = R^2 (1-B^2)/(4 kappa (1-kappa)), kappa = R H;  join on the sphere iff 1-B^2 <= 4 kappa (1-kappa);  equator join at kappa = (1+B)/2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.2748/tmj/1178229688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.10.e87457>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.28816> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Constant-Mean-Curvature Surfaces of Revolution (Delaunay 1841 / Plateau catalogue: sphere, cylinder, unduloid, nodoid, catenoid) — geometric" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.flask_equator_join" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_211.flask_join_feasible" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
